          <caption>
            <p>Boutonniere Deformity Anatomy. The diagram illustrates the permanent flexion of the proximal interphalangeal joint. The distal interphalangeal joint simultaneously exhibits hyperextension due to a ruptured central slip of the extensor tendon. Contributed by S Bhmiji, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="boutonniere" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
